# L §6.1 Writes into members: "Currencies are one by their code ... Any other unit a member declares is its own
# (a.hour)". Members a and b each declare a unit hour (with different labels, which no longer meet): a's hours are
# a.hour, b's b.hour. The joint model reads a.h as 3 a.hour; a's ask, asked as a.q, answers as a alone does (3 hour).
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "a.tally" sha256 "44caa3b76989672d221a267a273bfc71bbb8aa4d2e1e066a3252ca68ff56ac8e"
  use b = "b.tally" sha256 "13a6cdb10a29da422534df9445eb455a8adb8b20fb8679806abb92ead03318cd"

ask r: a.h
=== a.tally
model a
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

unit hour "godzina"

input h: num hour

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  h = 3 hour "umowa"

ask q: h
=== b.tally
model b
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"

unit hour "hour of work"

input h: num hour

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  h = 5 hour "umowa"

ask q: h
=== expect r a.q
r: 3 a.hour
  cut 2026-10-20
a.q: 3 hour
  cut 2026-10-20
